# Against the hand-run sweep in goodfeatures-x86_64.log, same host, same binary,
# same pinning, on the OpenCV binarized / binCV streaming ratio:
#
#   hand-run    median 1.1346   95% CI [1.1120, 1.1537]   +/- 1.84%
#   this sweep  median 1.1297   95% CI [1.1147, 1.1684]   +/- 2.38%
#   pooled, 60  median 1.1317   95% CI [1.1181, 1.1454]   +/- 1.20%
#
# The two medians are 0.4% apart, well inside what either sweep says it can
# resolve, and each interval contains the other's median. That is the protocol
# reproducing -- and it is the thing a single launch cannot do: the two sweeps'
# individual launches range from 0.856 to 1.605.

